WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.590
- I want to ask you, speaking of music.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.550
So Allie, right?

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:03.383
Your daughter.
- Yes!

00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.804
She's she's now doing the
whole music scene, right?

00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:06.910
- She worships you too as
every female singer does.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.210
- Oh, I remember meeting her.
- Yes.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.043
And she was so lovely.

00:00:09.043 --> 00:00:10.580
I think she was coming
from soccer practice

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.090
when I ran into her and I
was doing Trisha's thing.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.680
- What are you laughing at?
- I think, I think it was.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.760
No, I know, and I was like,

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.670
oh, we're like so similar.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.040
Like things she said,
because I played soccer too.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.780
But anyway, but I
remember meeting her and,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.800
her whole thing was music.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.710
So, now she's doing it.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.640
- Yeah you two guys remind
me scarily of each other

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.440
because one, both of
you can sing anything,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.170
but what kills me is neither one of you

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.810
seem to ever wear out.
- Oh.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.700
- It's like two o'clock in the morning.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.546
She's still, she's just still going.

00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:36.379
- Oh.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:38.900
- Wake up, she goes,
and you guys are just--

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.520
- Literally my makeup
artists just told me that

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.524
yesterday in the church,

00:00:41.524 --> 00:00:43.678
she was like, I don't know
where you'd get all the energy.

00:00:43.678 --> 00:00:44.511
I was like--

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.200
- Okay, so let's talk about
this if we can, right quick.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.050
First of all, hats off.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.816
Unbelievable job at the Billboard Awards.

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:52.080
- Oh!
- Now, come on, man.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:52.960
You're sitting there.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.362
You're sitting there
- You too!

00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:57.950
with no crowd whatsoever
and you're giving 1000%.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:58.980
- You did that!

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.760
- Well, I gotta tell you.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.750
You know this in entertainment.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.110
There's two parts of entertainment,

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.210
a great entrance and a great exit.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.140
So, Cher, of all people,
- Yeah.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.680
gives you the entrance,
- Yeah.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.770
but afterward that place is empty

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.420
except you come on and go,
yeah, that just happened!

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.253
Melt your face!
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:16.253 --> 00:01:17.980
And you pushed the crowd button

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.853
and it was like, oh thank you.

00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:20.810
Because you bookend it.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.050
And you made me look a
lot better than I am.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.511
But you made me look like--

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:28.110
- Oh, you shut your face!
- The Icon Award, it was good.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.060
- I'm going to be real with you.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.927
Whenever I got the script, I was like,

00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:33.510
he doesn't have the Icon Award yet?

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.435
I was like, what were we waiting for?

00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:37.597
- It's very (indistinct).

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.040
- That was kind of the crazy thing to me.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.560
- I think there could
have been a hundred guys,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.010
but Robert Deaton, thank God, was,

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:42.900
you know, directing.
- Yeah.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.970
- And he's the guy called
me and I just said,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.610
thank you for Country Music.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.161
- But you did an amazing job.

00:01:48.161 --> 00:01:49.943
- Thank you.
- There was no crowd there.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.776
It was just the crew that
you were performing for.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:51.609
- We brought our crowd with us.

00:01:51.609 --> 00:01:53.020
We brought the 80,000 people.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.610
We got the fans singing.
- That's so awesome.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.443
- All this stuff.

00:01:55.443 --> 00:01:57.550
It was so good. And man, again,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.970
thanks for the opportunity because

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.780
what you don't realize,
these guys understand it.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.150
You don't get to play anymore.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.040
- Amen.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.756
- You don't get to play more.
- I'm lucky.

00:02:05.756 --> 00:02:07.640
- So any chance that you
get to sing and play,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.550
thank you God.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.900
Thank you people that do the Zoom stuff.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.460
It's a chance to get to see.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.770
- You're like me, the zoom stuff.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:14.910
I'm not techy either.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.390
(laughs)
- I love it.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.700
- But do you know how to run it all?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.533
I don't.

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:19.950
- No.
- Okay, me neither!

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.000
- I do know how to look in
there and go, I see those faces.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.160
I see those faces at every live show,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.111
you know, and you can
see them right there.

00:02:29.111 --> 00:02:29.944
You can see the depth in them.

00:02:29.944 --> 00:02:31.540
You can see their heart and soul.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.252
- Oh!
- It's sweet.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.281
- You know what?
- It is!

00:02:35.281 --> 00:02:37.438
- And everyone gets touched
easily right now as well,

00:02:37.438 --> 00:02:38.370
because we are like,

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.990
and now it's like, you
know, booming again.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.460
Everything's in red and it's like, gosh,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.670
everybody just wants to be around people.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.740
And it's the hardest thing.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:45.790
- You see this because

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.590
the sad thing is everyone
gets the same view.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.380
So nobody knows exactly
who I'm talking to.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:51.340
- In the lovely green.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.640
- But it's the lady in green.
- Like an emerald.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.770
- That sits there, that gets it.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.570
It's like, oh my God, man,

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.040
how lucky we are to get
to be together this way.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.740
But just think, it's like
pulling that arrow back.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.430
The more you keep us apart.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.263
- Oh my God.

00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:07.725
It's going to be like Woodstock.

00:03:07.725 --> 00:03:08.558
(laughing)

00:03:08.558 --> 00:03:10.510
I swear to God, I'm
going to be in the front,

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.343
like, going woo!

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.970
I'm going to be so excited.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:14.970
- It's going to be so good.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.730
And there's going to be
800 artists like me and you

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.740
go get the hell out of my way,

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.240
because I want to get on that stage.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.370
And I want to hear those voices.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.660
- There's not going to be enough stages.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.290
We're just going to start
playing like tailgate,

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.054
like parking lots.

00:03:26.054 --> 00:03:27.810
- I tell you what, I'm sure
you got a million gigs,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.440
but my stage is big enough for both of us.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.310
- Oh my gosh!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.270
- It's not big enough for your voice,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.050
but we'll add on.
- No, I freaked out

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.990
when I got to come out and I sang

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.478
and it was with Trisha.

00:03:37.478 --> 00:03:39.140
It was amazing, anyway.
- It was fun.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.730
- It was, and I never
got to see those shows

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.563
when I was a kid.

00:03:41.563 --> 00:03:45.527
So, it's insane because
for me playing big arenas,

00:03:45.527 --> 00:03:47.680
I'm such a theater kid at heart,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.730
or like a club girl at heart,

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.530
I love the intimacy of it.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.270
So, it's not so easy for me

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.780
to bring it in and you do such a good job.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.910
Annie Lennox does such
a good job of that too.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:57.743
- She's a monster.

00:03:57.743 --> 00:03:58.930
- It's like, y'all just bring it in.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.487
Anyway, I was, I was really impressed.

00:04:00.487 --> 00:04:01.320
- I love Annie.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.840
- But since you're not touring,
what have you been doing?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.805
- Whatever Ms. Yearwood tells me to.

00:04:04.805 --> 00:04:05.700
(laughing)

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.120
So, the honeydew list, I swear to God,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:07.953
I don't know.

00:04:07.953 --> 00:04:08.786
It's like in the middle of the night,

00:04:08.786 --> 00:04:10.670
she must add to it because
I'll wake up in the morning.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.860
It's just like four
times longer than it was.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.980
But you know, we're lucky
enough to be on a farm,

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.947
every blade of grass on that farm.

00:04:17.947 --> 00:04:20.580
(laughing)

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.980
- It's manicured!

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:25.140
So it's, you know, you
just kinda keep going.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.313
You kind of quarantine,

00:04:28.002 --> 00:04:30.430
Miss Yearwood said she thinks
she was born for quarantine.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.630
Because she loves getting on
the couch, drinking her coffee,

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.940
reading a book and she
can, she can isolate.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.773
- Yeah.

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:38.470
- But I think she can isolate
because she's Trisha Yearwood.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.762
What, I'd love to isolate
with Trisha Yearwood.

00:04:40.762 --> 00:04:42.152
- I would too.

00:04:42.152 --> 00:04:43.657
So, next quarantine invite me over.

00:04:43.657 --> 00:04:45.110
But I hear so on your farm,

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.780
I saw you have a bruised finger.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.650
Didn't you hurt yourself?

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.030
- Oh, yeah just about a month ago.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.400
This thing happened, a
stupid thing, it's my fault.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.233
I was tired.

00:04:53.357 --> 00:04:54.190
But the knuckle's coming down,

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.640
just about time to get
the wedding ring back on.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.473
So sorry, honey,

00:04:56.473 --> 00:04:57.660
but it usually goes there,

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.590
but all I'm going to end
up doing is losing a nail.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.200
And I got to tell you when it happened,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.150
I just looked up at the sky, it was dark

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.750
because you know, we'd
worked way too long,

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:05.720
us loading the truck.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.470
And I just took my right
hand and just said,

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.916
please just let me have him.

00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:10.749
- Yeah.

00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:12.215
- Just let me have him, please.

00:05:12.215 --> 00:05:13.410
And they were pretty busted up.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.283
- As a musician, that's
gotta be a little terrifying.

00:05:15.283 --> 00:05:16.876
- It'd be okay if it was on this hand.

00:05:16.876 --> 00:05:18.227
- Yeah, that's what I'm saying!

00:05:18.227 --> 00:05:19.060
- This one.
- Yeah.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:19.893
- And so, yeah.

00:05:19.893 --> 00:05:22.570
So when we play today, I might
be doing this chord a lot.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:23.850
- You're going to flip me off a lot?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:24.683
Cool.
- So, I'm so sorry.

00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:26.067
It's called the F chord.
- I'm here for the bird.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.427
(laughing)

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:28.404
It's called the F chord?

00:05:28.404 --> 00:05:29.500
It's called the F chord because
it hurts so bad to play,

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.170
but it's a chance to get to play, man.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.770
I'm looking so forward to today.

